546875], "id": 59, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.42.0", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "ResolutionSelector"}, "order": 3}, {"outputs": [{"name": "CONDITIONING", "links": [92, 96], "label": "CONDITIONING", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "CONDITIONING"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": ["Create a complete Chinese newspaper front page as a flat, full-bleed editorial layout. The image itself IS the newspaper page: its outer boundaries are exactly the boundaries of the newspaper design. All typography, photographs, rules and columns are printed directly across this canvas. No tabletop, surrounding environment, visible sheet edges, curled corners, perspective distortion, cast shadows or newspaper mockup.\n\nUse a pale warm-gray newsprint background with very subtle paper fibers. Black ink, restrained dark-red divider rules, authentic Chinese newspaper typography and precise editorial alignment. The layout contains a very large masthead, a bold main headline, a medium subtitle, a small byline, one large news photograph, a small photo caption and a complete article in two columns. Every text block must remain readable, with consistent margins and clear spacing.\n\nAt the top, the oversized masthead reads exactly:\n“街巷周报”\n\nDirectly below, a small publication line reads exactly:\n“社区生活版｜第028期｜星期五”\n\nA thin dark-red horizontal rule separates the masthead from the lead story.\n\nThe large bold black headline reads exactly:\n“老街书屋亮起夜读灯”\n\nThe medium-sized subtitle reads exactly:\n“二十四个座位，留住下班后的一小时”\n\nThe small byline reads exactly:\n“本报记者 林晓 文／摄”\n\nBelow the headline area, place one large rectangular documentary news photograph spanning the width of the article. This photograph is an image printed within the newspaper layout. It shows a renovated Chinese neighborhood reading room at dusk: old timber beams, tall bookshelves, a large street-facing window and a long wooden table illuminated by warm reading lamps. An elderly reader sits at the left, a parent and child share a picture book near the center, and an adult woman reads quietly at the right. A volunteer works behind a service desk in the background. Cool evening light outside contrasts with the warm interior. Natural candid expressions, believable hands and books, muted documentary colors and a subtle printed halftone texture. No readable signs appear inside the photograph.\n\nImmediately beneath the photograph, the small caption reads exactly:\n“图为居民在青禾社区书屋阅读，夜间开放让老街多了一处温暖去处。”\n\nThe lower portion of the page contains the complete report in two balanced columns of small, crisp Chinese Song-style type. Place the first two paragraphs in the left column and the final two paragraphs in the right column. Read top to bottom within each column, then continue into the next column. Use consistent line spacing, a clear central gutter and modest first-line indentation. Reproduce the following article verbatim, preserving every character and punctuation mark:\n\n本报讯 傍晚七点，青禾街的沿街商铺陆续收摊，一间临街书屋却刚刚迎来热闹时刻。经过两个月整理与修缮，青禾社区书屋本周重新开放，并首次将闭馆时间延长至晚上九点，为下班后的居民留出安静阅读的空间。\n\n书屋由一处闲置老店铺改造而成，保留了原有木梁和临街大窗，新增二十四个阅读座位。首批上架图书约三千册，涵盖文学、历史、少儿读物和生活技能。靠窗区域设有共享长桌，读者可免费阅读，也可凭登记信息办理借阅。\n\n“以前下班回家，总是拿起手机就停不下来。现在能在这里坐半小时，心里踏实多了。”附近居民陈女士说。开放首日，有家长陪孩子读绘本，也有老人翻阅地方文史资料。志愿者在服务台协助登记，并为初次到访的居民介绍借阅规则。\n\n社区负责人介绍，书屋将试行一个月夜间开放，期间每周五举办一次小型共读活动。后续将根据到访人数和读者反馈调整安排，同时征集居民希望补充的书目。书屋也提醒读者保持安静、爱护图书，让这盏夜读灯成为邻里共享的日常风景。\n\nAt the bottom, a thin horizontal rule separates the article from the small footer:\n“街巷观察 · 记录身边的变化”\n\nPlace the page number “01” at the bottom right.\n\nThe final result is the finished newspaper page design itself, filling the entire image. Keep the complete report visible, with large and small typography clearly distinguished, no clipped paragraphs, no duplicated sentences, no placeholder text and no additional invented wording."], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 88, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name